# backend/.env.example — copy to .env.personal for per-developer overrides:
#   cp .env.example .env.personal
#
# Shared local config (Postgres creds, SECRETS_ENCRYPTION_KEY) lives — encrypted — in the committed
# .env.local.enc. You do NOT set those here; you only need the private key to decrypt them. Get
# backend/.env.keys (DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY_LOCAL_ENC) from 1Password and drop it in backend/. Then:
#   docker compose up -d postgres redis && pnpm install && pnpm db:recreate
#
# Anything in .env.personal OVERRIDES the shared .env.local.enc (dotenvx `-o`). Use it for personal
# secrets and machine-specific overrides only. NODE_ENV is set by the runtime, never in a dotenv file.
#
# The typed env contract is backend/src/_core/config/env/validation.ts. Env vars are for values that
# differ per environment or are secrets — constant tuning knobs (timeouts, windows, limits) live in
# code, not here. Vars are REQUIRED by default; a few diverge by env and are optional.

# ─── Required for the app to boot (shared dev values are in .env.local.enc / set your own here) ───
# POSTGRES_HOST, POSTGRES_USER, POSTGRES_PASSWORD, POSTGRES_DB   (+ POSTGRES_PORT, default 5432)
# SECRETS_ENCRYPTION_KEY   — AES key for secrets-at-rest
# JWT_ACCESS_SECRET, JWT_REFRESH_SECRET   — the global auth guard needs these
# JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=
# JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=

# ─── Optional: diverge by environment ───
# POSTGRES_SSL_MODE   — disable | require | verify-full (defaults by NODE_ENV: disable local, verify-full prod)
# REDIS_URL           — unset → redis://127.0.0.1:6379; local compose Redis is on :6380
# SANDBOX_REDIS_URL   — the SAME Redis as REDIS_URL, but reachable FROM INSIDE the k3d pod (the engine runs there,
#                       so a host `localhost` won't resolve). On k3d use the host alias: redis://host.k3d.internal:6380
# COOKIE_DOMAIN       — host-only in dev (unset); scopes cookies across subdomains in deploy
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6380
# SANDBOX_REDIS_URL=redis://host.k3d.internal:6380

# ─── Optional: dev-only admin seed (provisions an approved admin on boot; unset → no auto-seed) ───
# ADMIN_SEED_EMAIL=you@example.com
# ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD=change-me

# ─── Not in the typed schema — read directly from process.env (leave unset to disable) ───
# LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY / LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY / LANGFUSE_BASE_URL / LANGFUSE_TRACING_ENVIRONMENT  — tracing
# ENABLE_COLOR=true / ENABLE_TIMESTAMP=true  — logger output toggles
